      "type": "item",
      "section": "Security, misuse & threat intelligence",
      "headline": "US seizes infrastructure behind North Korean 'FaceStealer' campaign that stole more than $400 million in cryptocurrency",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "Staying with BleepingComputer, and this one is an update — the vendor research behind it was published before our window opened." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "The US government has seized the infrastructure behind a North Korean social engineering campaign called FaceStealer. BleepingComputer says it stole more than $400 million in cryptocurrency, ran for 18 months, and that authorities identified more than 900 webcam videos the hackers secretly recorded of tech workers." },
