      "type": "item",
      "section": "Research & papers",
      "headline": "Preprint reports 5.85x decoding speedup for looped transformers, 40% above the strongest baseline on Ouro-2.6B",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "On research, the edition notes that arXiv ran no announcement cycle inside our window at all." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "There's still a preprint to report. On alphaXiv, submitted November 14th, a paper called LoopFill reports an average speedup over greedy autoregressive decoding of 5.85 times on Ouro-2.6B and 5.13 times on Huginn-3.5B, averaged across seven benchmarks." },
